>> title: Barbecue Slaw
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: cabbage, vinegar, barbecue, side, no-cook
>> counters: Smokehouse
>> aka: red slaw, dip slaw, Lexington slaw, bbq slaw, barbeque slaw
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 20 min
>> pairs-with: chopped-pork, hush-puppies

>> step: whisk the dressing
Whisk @tomato ketchup{1/2%cup}(135 g), @cider vinegar{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @granulated sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g), @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @coarse black pepper{1%tsp}, and @red pepper flakes{1%tsp} into a dressing.

>> step: chop fine
Chop @green cabbage{2%lb}(900 g; cored) fine on a #board{}, close to minced.

>> step: toss
Toss @&(~1)chopped cabbage{} with @&(~2)dressing{} and @yellow onion{2%Tbs}(grated).

>> step: chill 1 hr
Chill @&(~1)slaw{} for ~chill{1%hr}, until the cabbage has taken the colour and softened.
